{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ","id":1220735,"title":"The Anti-Christ","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-20T23:22:28-07:00","id":1220735,"title":"The Anti-Christ","content":"So. The World of Darkness is mainly judeo Christian on it's Mythos And lore.<br /> <br /> I suspected that every splat must have some Anti christ figure, i mean. I can picture nephandi trying to make one at least every once a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:36:53-07:00","id":1220739,"title":"","content":"This debatable, even in a setting like Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:40:04-07:00","id":1220741,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: Perfect Metis<br /> Vampires: mostly Caine and maybe the Antediluvians<br /> Mage: there was this first Nephandus guy in revised<br /> Changeling: Balor (or, for some, High King David <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> Demon: Well, guess what? There's actually a whole bunch of them running around.<br /> <br /> Any more?<br /> <br /> Also, the main reason the World of Darkness is &quot;judeo christian&quot; in it's lore is because the creators were pretty america-centric in the first editions. Good thing all the christian roots get pretty much debunked (even in Demon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T00:33:20-07:00","id":1220751,"title":"","content":"America-centrism wasn't a factor. Vampire was made to have a cosmology based off the Bible be design, it want unintentional bias. Most of the following game lives weren't remotely Judeo-Christian, with Demon being the big exception. <br /> <br /> Anyway, there are any number of ways you could have an Anti-Christ figure in a WoD game. My concern would be that either he would be so powerful that his actions might remove player agency or, if players can affect him, he is underwhelming. The Anti-Christ is associated with the Appcalypse, so I would imagine that this would involve some kind of end of the world scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T01:12:11-07:00","id":1220756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1220751#post1220751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">America-centrism wasn't a factor. Vampire was made to have a cosmology based off the Bible be design, it want unintentional bias. Most of the following game lives weren't remotely Judeo-Christian, with Demon being the big exception.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are any number of ways you could have an Anti-Christ figure in a WoD game. My concern would be that either he would be so powerful that his actions might remove player agency or, if players can affect him, he is underwhelming. The Anti-Christ is associated with the Appcalypse, so I would imagine that this would involve some kind of end of the world scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The antichrist of the Bible isn't meant to be super powerful. They are meant to be a warning about people who claim they are working in Jesus' name when they are doing horrible things. So probably anyone on Road of Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:33:06-07:00","id":1220827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1220756#post1220756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The antichrist of the Bible isn't meant to be super powerful. They are meant to be a warning about people who claim they are working in Jesus' name when they are doing horrible things. So probably anyone on Road of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Vampire, it's even more likely someone on a path of the Road of Sin pretending to be on a path from the Road of Heaven all while getting the world to do terrible things with calls of unity and togetherness as though these actions are Christian in nature. He's going to be popular* and if people interfere with his designs or in some way attack him, droves of fans, acolytes, and people in power are going to come down hard on the interlopers if said interlopers aren't careful about how they enact their plans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Presence, a smattering of Dominate, some Obfuscate**, and the ability to find an individual's moral failings with Daimoinon, anyone?<br /> **For the devastating combo disciplines like Memory Rift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:02:36-07:00","id":1221307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ#post1220735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. The World of Darkness is mainly judeo Christian on it's Mythos And lore.<br /> <br /> I suspected that every splat must have some Anti christ figure, i mean. I can picture nephandi trying to make one at least every once a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Vampire and Demon are. The other games are varying degrees of distant from the very much Protestant American cosmology of those two. Even the Perfect Metis is subject to the same Rule of Splatter as any other Garou character, and there are other figures of dread in Garou legend and prophecy to be found, none of whom really have the kind of presentation that Revelations did in its coded dissing of Nero Caesar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T02:20:02-07:00","id":1221424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1220756#post1220756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The antichrist of the Bible isn't meant to be super powerful. They are meant to be a warning about people who claim they are working in Jesus' name when they are doing horrible things. So probably anyone on Road of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is only accurate if you are assuming a non-literal reading of the bible. Plenty of people think the figure in the Revelations of John is an actual, living, breathing Satanic figure that will come to rule over an age of darkness; this interpretation is almost certainly what OP and Sergeant Brother are referring to.<br /> <br /> If this literal Antichrist is real, he is going to be powerful, and in ways that are temporal and tangible... unlike, say, Christ, who seems like an itinerate Jewish nobody. The Antichrist is supposed to rule a united world government, recover easily from mortal injuries and be invested with the powers of hell. Unless you and your group want to run a game of The Omen: All Grown Up, taking out the Antichrist should not be straightforward or easy.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T15:42:37-07:00","id":1221861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1221424#post1221424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is only accurate if you are assuming a non-literal reading of the bible. Plenty of people think the figure in the Revelations of John is an actual, living, breathing Satanic figure that will come to rule over an age of darkness; this interpretation is almost certainly what OP and Sergeant Brother are referring to.<br /> <br /> If this literal Antichrist is real, he is going to be powerful, and in ways that are temporal and tangible... unlike, say, Christ, who seems like an itinerate Jewish nobody. The Antichrist is supposed to rule a united world government, recover easily from mortal injuries and be invested with the powers of hell. Unless you and your group want to run a game of The Omen: All Grown Up, taking out the Antichrist should not be straightforward or easy.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, a litteral reading of the Bible has very specific statements where the phrase &quot;Antichrist&quot; and &quot;false Messiah&quot; are stated. They are not used in reference to the Beast of the Earth. That there is a super monster in Revelations(and Daniel) has nothing to do with the class of person known as antichrists. There are comments on &quot;The lawless One&quot; as well but also not phrased as Anti or Psuedo christs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T07:57:00-07:00","id":1222413,"title":"","content":"As Lian is saying. There are many antichrists mentioned in the Bible who are those that work against the teachings of Christ.<br /> <br /> The Antichrist, mentioned in Revelation and Daniel however is much different in that he is possessed by Satan himself. This antichrist would be unkillable, and recovers from a mortal wound leading many to worship him. Biblically he doesn't die but is instead cast alive into the Lake of Fire with the False Prophet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T12:02:36-07:00","id":1222480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222413#post1222413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Lian is saying. There are many antichrists mentioned in the Bible who are those that work against the teachings of Christ.<br /> <br /> The Antichrist, mentioned in Revelation and Daniel however is much different in that he is possessed by Satan himself. This antichrist would be unkillable, and recovers from a mortal wound leading many to worship him. Biblically he doesn't die but is instead cast alive into the Lake of Fire with the False Prophet.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is never called the Antichrist in the bible. The creatures in Revelations and Daniel have a variety of names but NEVER Antichrist. The focus on them as &quot;THE&quot; antichrist completely undercuts the whole message of the many antichrists that surround us constantly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T13:14:10-07:00","id":1222495,"title":"","content":"Trinity and rapture are never mentioned it the bible either so semantics aren't the issue. He's refere to as the beast in Revelation but in study and discussion the beast is normally referred to as the antichrist. In the gospels Jesus mentions many antichrists are to come, but in common discussions the term antichrist almost always refers to the beast of Revelation. Just as I believe the OP is doing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T15:37:29-07:00","id":1222530,"title":"","content":"What are we even talking about? OP is talking about the kid from the Omen, not everyone past, present or future that disagrees with the teachings of Christ. The former is a scary quasi-folkloric supernaturally possessed thing colloquially referred to as the Antichrist, and some people even believe something like that is foretold in the Bible.<br /> <br /> The latter, mundane interpretation of 'Antichrist' isn't even worth discussing as an enemy of vampires or werewolves, since they are just normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T16:04:19-07:00","id":1222538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222495#post1222495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trinity and rapture are never mentioned it the bible either so semantics aren't the issue. He's refere to as the beast in Revelation but in study and discussion the beast is normally referred to as the antichrist. In the gospels Jesus mentions many antichrists are to come, but in common discussions the term antichrist almost always refers to the beast of Revelation. Just as I believe the OP is doing</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Rapture is also complete bullshit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222530#post1222530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are we even talking about? OP is talking about the kid from the Omen, not everyone past, present or future that disagrees with the teachings of Christ. The former is a scary quasi-folkloric supernaturally possessed thing colloquially referred to as the Antichrist, and some people even believe something like that is foretold in the Bible.<br /> <br /> The latter, mundane interpretation of 'Antichrist' isn't even worth discussing as an enemy of vampires or werewolves, since they are just normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except is in all ways more useful as there's nothing anything but the most epic of pcs could do to fight the Beast of Revelations. But to use werewolf for example one could easily use servants of the wyrm who couch themselves in trapping of Gaia as a threat. Either explicitly or those garou so caught in power and personal desire all the while saying &quot;FOR GAIA&quot; and using it against their political enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T16:26:59-07:00","id":1222542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222538#post1222538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rapture is also complete bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably shouldn't even go here, especially in this thread, but I was wondering what brought out this statement and why. If it's because you dismiss the Bible as such then then there's no point in the discussion. If this is only how you feel about the Rapture itself then we have grounds for discussion. Though probably in another thread or in PMs.<br /> <br /> Either way I do agree with the remainder of you post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Spelling 05-27-2018, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T22:42:36-07:00","id":1222583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222538#post1222538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except is in all ways more useful as there's nothing anything but the most epic of pcs could do to fight the Beast of Revelations. But to use werewolf for example one could easily use servants of the wyrm who couch themselves in trapping of Gaia as a threat. Either explicitly or those garou so caught in power and personal desire all the while saying &quot;FOR GAIA&quot; and using it against their political enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of the sticking points of Dark Alliance: Vancouver and the &quot;Priest of Gaia&quot;, though it was only one option for where the ST could steer things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T17:41:26-07:00","id":1222761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222542#post1222542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I probably shouldn't even go here, especially in this thread, but I was wondering what brought out this statement and why. If it's because you dismiss the Bible as such then then there's no point in the discussion. If this is only how you feel about the Rapture itself then we have grounds for discussion. Though probably in another thread or in PMs.<br /> <br /> Either way I do agree with the remainder of you post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Dismiss completely and utterly the rapture has having any basis in the bible. It is a wholesale creation of 19th century American Christianity. I also don't agree with the message in the bible about antichrists is the same as the messages in Daniel and Revelations. That in focusing on a &quot;ANTICHRIST&quot; vs the dangers of regular antichrists the message has been completely missed.<br /> <br /> But to bring that back on topic. I don't think a Super Evil character really has much applicable use in a game. What can you do when fighting Damien? Do you win because you're an actual monster? I mean the Omen is scary but imagine a pack of Garou vs little Damien.. its.. a much shorter movie! Really same thing with just about any set of supernaturals. You could of course power him up make him unstoppable for the monsters but then what? Or do you have some middle ground where its just as hard for the Monsters to fight Damien as mortals? <br /> <br /> It doesn't seem like there's really as much there as say going with false prophets especially among the garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T11:56:41-07:00","id":1255823,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't all of the non-Reconciler Fallen be considered Antichrist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T13:15:41-07:00","id":1257011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222761#post1222761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can you do when fighting Damien? Do you win because you're an actual monster? I mean the Omen is scary but imagine a pack of Garou vs little Damien.. its.. a much shorter movie! Really same thing with just about any set of supernaturals. You could of course power him up make him unstoppable for the monsters but then what? Or do you have some middle ground where its just as hard for the Monsters to fight Damien as mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going just by the movies, even werewolves would apparently need to gather the Seven Daggers of Megiddo to do lil' Damien any real harm. And would not be immune to all the &quot;coincidental&quot; accidents that seemed to surround him, though they'd stand much better chances of surviving some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T14:14:07-07:00","id":1257024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1257011#post1257011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going just by the movies, even werewolves would apparently need to gather the Seven Daggers of Megiddo to do lil' Damien any real harm. And would not be immune to all the &quot;coincidental&quot; accidents that seemed to surround him, though they'd stand much better chances of surviving some of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Yeah, there was some hiccup with a car accident, but I managed to step sideways before it hit. Funny that this business never seems to happen in the Umbra...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T18:59:44-08:00","id":1282367,"title":"","content":"If I dust off my Nostradamus there are three Anti-Christs: Napoleon, Hitler and Abbas. Abbas has yet to appear and Nostradamus also calls him the lord of the blue helmet. The blue helmet could be that of a UN peacekeeper meaning that Abbas is working as one and making contacts with military contractors and other power players even now. The blue helmet could also be the crown Yul Brynner wore in &quot;The Ten Commandments&quot;. I think it's already established as World of Darkness lore that a number of super-naturals were brought under Hitler's influence, so there is precedence for others to fall under the sway of Abbas. If you read the conspiracy books of Jim Marrs you know that both the Russian revolution and the Nazis were financed by the Rockefeller Foundation, so look to see who in Iraq is taking money from the Rockefeller Foundation and you have a good idea of were the next Anti-Christ is going to arise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T16:21:00-08:00","id":1282539,"title":"","content":"I present to you the AntiChrist of all splats, rolled in to one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Samuel_Haight\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Samuel_Haight</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T18:01:40-08:00","id":1282561,"title":"","content":"How about Saulot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T19:18:21-08:00","id":1282567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1222480#post1222480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He is never called the Antichrist in the bible. The creatures in Revelations and Daniel have a variety of names but NEVER Antichrist. The focus on them as &quot;THE&quot; antichrist completely undercuts the whole message of the many antichrists that surround us constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the Bible does call him by these other epithets; The Little Horn. The Lawless One. The Man of Sin. The Son of Perdition. The Beast from the Sea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T19:38:09-08:00","id":1282568,"title":"","content":"Don't forget; even if we assume the Bible was granted by a divine being to a Prophet and infallible originally. (I don't, but even if you do)<br /> It has been imperfectly translated through countless versions by fallible humans, often with their own motives.<br /> <br /> How about looking at the general pop-culture theme of an antichrist than trying to argue what a multigenerational tome created with stories between 2000 and 3000 years ago means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T15:16:20-08:00","id":1284405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1220735-the-anti-christ?p=1282568#post1282568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget; even if we assume the Bible was granted by a divine being to a Prophet and infallible originally. (I don't, but even if you do)<br /> It has been imperfectly translated through countless versions by fallible humans, often with their own motives.<br /> <br /> How about looking at the general pop-culture theme of an antichrist than trying to argue what a multigenerational tome created with stories between 2000 and 3000 years ago means?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little rusty on Demon but if I remember correctly one of the books suggested that it might have actually been Lucifer who founded Abrahamic religions in an eventually successful attempt to wrest power away from the Earthbound.<br /> <br /> I also remember in one of the books they talk about the Nephilim really vaguely, so if someone were the 'Antichrist' in the sense that he's the son of Lucifer, I think it would be one of those. I have no idea how that would come about, but that's the closest thing I can imagine as the Antichrist. Maybe imagine a Mage who can make pacts and has all the innate powers that the fallen possess? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6149-malfean90","name":"Malfean90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T15:50:49-08:00","id":1284592,"title":"","content":"From what I have gauged, Nephilim seem to be considered antithetical to God's design, so a good candidate as an Antichrist. (Especially if you look at Jesus being conceived of Angel and Mortal, then the Antichrist being Demon and Mortal born makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T13:41:53-08:00","id":1288716,"title":"","content":"An alternative scenario for the anti-Christ is presented by Mark Booth in &quot;The Secret History of the World&quot; pg. 539. &quot;...Satan will incarnate. He will do so as a writer. His aim will be to destroy spirituality by 'explaining it away'. He will have the ability to create supernatural events, but then know how to give them a reductively scientific explanation.&quot;<br /> <br /> That to me sounds like the technocracy, though you might be able to stretch it to cover Demon the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}